  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "overview",
      "type": "overview",
      "label": "Start",
      "title": "The case history",
      "learn": [
        "A written case history tells the story in the Präteritum. Er kam, sah und sagte. ich and er share that form.",
        "Weak verbs add -te: sagen → sagte, machen → machte. A stem in -t or -d adds -ete: warten → wartete. Not sagete, and not wartte.",
        "Strong verbs change the vowel and add no -te: kommen → kam, sehen → sah, gehen → ging, geben → gab, bleiben → blieb, schreiben → schrieb, trinken → trank, messen → maß.",
        "Chapter 23 still has war and hatte for a state. Chapter 28 still uses the Perfekt for a finished action in a spoken progress note. Chapter 27 still has konnte. käme and ginge are not this past."
      ],
      "minutes": 25,
      "vocab": [
        { "de": "Patient", "article": "der", "plural": "die Patienten", "en": "patient (male)", "emoji": "🤒", "glossaryKey": "patient" },
        { "de": "Arzt", "article": "der", "plural": "die Ärzte", "en": "doctor (male)", "emoji": "👨‍⚕️", "glossaryKey": "arzt" },
        { "de": "Befund", "article": "der", "plural": "die Befunde", "en": "finding; report", "emoji": "📋", "glossaryKey": "befund" },
        { "de": "Bett", "article": "das", "plural": "die Betten", "en": "bed", "emoji": "🛏️", "image": { "type": "svg", "id": "bed" }, "glossaryKey": "bett" }
      ],
      "text": {
        "title": "Er kam, sah und sagte",
        "de": "Der Patient kam um acht. Der Arzt sah das Fieber. Der Patient sagte nichts und blieb im Bett. Anna schrieb den Befund. Die Pflegekraft wartete.",
        "en": "The patient came at eight. The doctor saw the fever. The patient said nothing and stayed in bed. Anna wrote the report. The nurse waited."
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "grammar",
      "type": "grammar",
      "label": "Grammar",
      "title": "kam, sah, sagte",
      "practice": "choose",
      "heroTitle": "Er kam, sah und sagte",
      "heroImage": "clipboard",
      "story": [
        "The case history is a written story, so the verbs stand in the <b>Präteritum</b>. <b>Er kam, sah und sagte.</b> On the ward: <b>Der Patient kam um acht. Der Arzt sah das Fieber. Der Patient sagte nichts.</b>",
        "Weak verbs add <b>-te</b>. sagen → <b>sagte</b>, machen → machte. ich and er share it. du adds -st: sagtest. wir, sie and Sie add -en: sagten. ihr adds -t: sagtet. A stem in -t or -d needs an extra e: warten → <b>wartete</b>. Not wartte. sagen does not take that e: not sagete.",
        "Strong verbs change the vowel and take <b>no -te</b>. kommen → <b>kam</b>, sehen → <b>sah</b>, gehen → <b>ging</b>, geben → <b>gab</b>, bleiben → <b>blieb</b>, schreiben → <b>schrieb</b>, trinken → <b>trank</b>, sprechen → sprach, messen → <b>maß</b>. du still adds -st: kamst. wir adds -en: kamen. ihr adds -t: kamt.",
        "Two known pasts stay put. A state is still <b>war</b> and <b>hatte</b>, as in chapter 23. A modal is still <b>konnte</b>, as in chapter 27. <b>käme</b> and <b>ginge</b> are not this narrative past, just as könnte is not the past of können.",
        "A spoken progress note, as in chapter 28, still uses the Perfekt for a finished action: hat gemessen, ist geblieben, ist gekommen. This chapter is the written story, so the same events are <b>maß</b>, <b>blieb</b> and <b>kam</b>. blieb takes <b>im Bett</b>, location. ging takes <b>ins Zimmer</b>, movement.",
        "schreiben takes the accusative: <b>Anna schrieb den Befund.</b> geben takes the accusative: Er gab eine Tablette. Clock time takes um: <b>um acht</b>."
      ],
      "questionRule": "Case history. Weak: -te, or -ete after t or d. Strong: a new vowel, no -te. ich and er share the form.",
      "tables": [
